{"name":"Good as Gold","hex":"#d3ba75","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"good as gold","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of an asset, of high and enduring value.","Of a person, very well-behaved (especially of a child); very good-hearted (especially of an adult)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/good_as_gold"}],"entries":[{"title":"Good as Gold (novel)","blocks":[{"text":"Good as Gold is the third novel written by Joseph Heller. Portions of it were printed in The New York Times in 1976, and in Playboy in April 1979. The book was published in late 1979. The dust jacket was illustrated by Paul Bacon."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Good_as_gold_1st_edition_cover.jpg/330px-Good_as_gold_1st_edition_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Good_as_Gold_(novel)","wikidata":"Q3282109"},{"title":"Good as Gold (Red Rockers album)","blocks":[{"text":"Good as Gold is the second full-length album from Red Rockers, released in 1983 on Columbia/415. It contained the single \"China\" which peaked at number 53 on the Billboard Hot 100. Other singles from the album were \"Til It All Falls Down\" and the title track, \"Good as Gold\". The music video for the song \"Good as Gold\" was filmed at the Alamo Village - the same location where John Wayne shot the film, The Alamo."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/73/Album_good_as_gold.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Good_as_Gold_(Red_Rockers_album)","wikidata":"Q5583080"},{"title":"Good","blocks":[{"text":"In most contexts, the concept of good denotes the conduct that should be preferred when posed with a choice between possible actions. Good is generally considered to be the opposite of evil. The meaning and etymology of the term and its associated translations among ancient and contemporary languages show substantial variation in its inflection and meaning, depending on circumstances of place and history, or of philosophical or religious context."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Good","wikidata":"Q15290"},{"title":"Gold","blocks":[{"text":"Gold is a chemical element; its chemical symbol is Au and atomic number 79. In its pure form, it is a bright-metallic-yellow, dense, soft, malleable, and ductile metal. Chemically, gold is a transition metal, a group 11 element, and one of the noble metals. It is one of the least reactive chemical elements, being the second lowest in the reactivity series, with only platinum ranked as less reactive. Gold is solid under standard conditions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/Gold-crystals.jpg/330px-Gold-crystals.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold","wikidata":"Q897"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/75/Red_Rockers_single_Good_As_Gold.jpg/250px-Red_Rockers_single_Good_As_Gold.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/75/Red_Rockers_single_Good_As_Gold.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/75/Red_Rockers_single_Good_As_Gold.jpg/250px-Red_Rockers_single_Good_As_Gold.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARed_Rockers_single_Good_As_Gold.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Lenz_Entwurf_zu_einem_Engel.jpg/250px-Lenz_Entwurf_zu_einem_Engel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/08/Lenz_Entwurf_zu_einem_Engel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campai